@startuml fig4_qualities
' Diagram 4 of the ISO/IEC 22989 pattern: the qualities, and what reaches
' beyond the AI subdomain.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: how a model states a quality of an AI system, and the two
' terms of clause 3.5 that are modelled as things rather than as measured
' values.
'
' The named individuals come from ISO22989-instances.ttl, which a model imports
' separately. A model taking only the pattern gets the classes without the
' vocabulary.
'
' Control is not shown here. Its entry sits in clause 3.5 with the terms
' below, but the definition says action, so the pattern models it as a
' function and diagram 1 carries it.
'
' Left out on purpose: everything of diagrams 1 to 3 except the three classes
' the qualities attach to.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

' ===================================================================
'  What a quality attaches to
' ===================================================================

class AISystem
class AIComponent
class Model

' ===================================================================
'  How a value is stated
' ===================================================================

class CharacteristicValue {
  dataProp: quantity
  dataProp: unit
}

class Characteristic {
  <<enum>>
  Robustness
  Reliability
  Availability
  Resilience
  Explainability
  Predictability
  Bias
  Trustworthiness
  Performance
}

' Three holders, one relation. Labelling every edge writes the same name three
' times into the same space, so only the middle one carries it.
AISystem    --> "*" CharacteristicValue
AIComponent --> "*" CharacteristicValue : hasCharacteristicValue
Model       --> "*" CharacteristicValue

CharacteristicValue --> "1" Characteristic : forCharacteristic

' The second way into the same class, and what separates a value that was
' measured from one that was set. A quality of clause 3.5 is established by a
' system and reached through forCharacteristic; a hyperparameter is chosen
' before a training and reaches its value through hasSetting.
class Hyperparameter
Hyperparameter --> "1" CharacteristicValue : hasSetting

' ===================================================================
'  The three terms modelled as things
' ===================================================================

class Controllability
class Risk

AISystem -left-> "*" Controllability : hasControllability
AISystem -left-> "*" Risk            : hasRisk

' Layout only.
AISystem -[hidden]right- AIComponent
AIComponent -[hidden]right- Model

@enduml
